From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Input: chipone-icnl9922c - avoid ABBA deadlock in panel_unpreparing

icnl9922c_panel_unpreparing() previously held ts->lock while calling
synchronous disable_irq(ts->spi->irq), while the threaded IRQ handler
icnl9922c_irq_handler() acquires ts->lock. When a touch IRQ fires right
as drm_panel_unprepare() runs during system suspend (dpm_prepare), both
threads deadlock permanently and hang suspend before GFP mask restrict.

Clear ts->running and ts->irq_enabled under ts->lock, drop ts->lock
before calling disable_irq(), then re-acquire ts->lock to release any
active touch slots.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c
index 6a5f5f6f9..d960b66bd 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/chipone_icnl9922c.c
@@ -730,14 +730,27 @@ static int icnl9922c_panel_unpreparing(struct drm_panel_follower *follower)
 {
 	struct icnl9922c_ts *ts = container_of(follower, struct icnl9922c_ts,
 					       panel_follower);
+	bool disable = false;
 
 	cancel_work_sync(&ts->fw_work);
+
 	mutex_lock(&ts->lock);
 	ts->running = false;
 	if (ts->irq_enabled) {
-		disable_irq(ts->spi->irq);
 		ts->irq_enabled = false;
+		disable = true;
 	}
+	mutex_unlock(&ts->lock);
+
+	/*
+	 * disable_irq() synchronizes with the threaded IRQ handler, which
+	 * acquires ts->lock; never call it while holding ts->lock or an
+	 * in-flight touch IRQ during panel unprepare deadlocks suspend.
+	 */
+	if (disable)
+		disable_irq(ts->spi->irq);
+
+	mutex_lock(&ts->lock);
 	if (ts->input) {
 		input_mt_sync_frame(ts->input);
 		input_sync(ts->input);
